# `M154f` / `C54` — the third `tflw.config` under `tests/.constructs/`, and it exists for the same
# structural reason as `viewport/`'s next door: the key it grades is project-wide, so setting it in
# the root config would change what every other plant's report contains.
#
# **What this plant grades is the KEY, not the level.** `C41` already proves the level changes what
# a `screenshot` step does — it runs `step-observables.tflw` twice and reads the step's own reported
# detail out of `report/results.json` at each. But both of those runs set the level with the
# **`--evidence` command-line flag**, and so does every other use of the level in this repository:
# `tests/api/identity/safety-redaction.tflw` is driven with `--evidence` at run time, and the root
# config's own comment says so in as many words. Before this file, `evidence` as a *config key* had
# **zero occurrences anywhere in this repository**. A key that the parser accepted and then dropped
# on the floor would have been completely invisible — which is precisely the defect `C42` was built
# to catch for `viewport`, found by writing the plant rather than by reading the code.
#
# `full` rather than a lower level because `full` is the only level at which a capture happens at
# all (`interpreter.ts` — "evidence ... captured only at `evidence full`"), so it is the level whose
# arrival is observable. The control is the same step under the root config, which sets no level and
# where the step reports `not captured (evidence level)` while still passing.
#
# **No `viewport` here, deliberately.** The grader reads the PNG's own IHDR and expects Playwright's
# 1280x720 default; a viewport key in this file would silently move that number and the two plants
# would grade each other instead of themselves.
defaults
  evidence full

env local default
  api "http://localhost:4001/v1"
  web "http://localhost:8090"
